{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3077","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3077","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3077\",\"parent_revision\":\"df003bd6b50c247795ef3a7c665a100a692f4e51\",\"root_revision\":\"7ea7f3a88c18a033260fc978945d4c117a4a22766ffe00a9eda1d8f7805bb2cb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-20\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`backlog_groom` (with `append=True`, the pattern used by grooming/RT-ICA agents to add entries to a section) has no idempotency or dedup guard against repeated near-identical writes. #2953 currently has 91 total sections and ~270,946 estimated tokens (`backlog_view(map=True)` output), including a \\\"Summary\\\" section with 80 entries. Several are near-identical duplicates back to back \u2014 e.g. four consecutive \\\"RT-ICA Snapshot: refactor: backlog_core's github_...\\\" entries with identical 258-token previews.\\n\\nRoot cause hypothesis: this item was groomed during the window when #2956 (`backlog_groom` writes invisible via `backlog_view`, fixed in PR #3040 / commit `6214055a`) was active. Grooming/RT-ICA agents could not confirm prior writes had landed, so they re-ran and re-appended full content each time instead of detecting an existing entry and replacing/skipping it.\\n\\n## Why this needs its own fix (separate from the #3054/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md work)\\n\\n`docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md` (R1\u2013R8) is explicitly scoped to *reading* markdown \u2014 item/plan/task/artifact views and listings. It says nothing about write-side append behavior. None of #3054's tracked children (#3057\u2013#3064, #3072\u2013#3076) touch grooming writes either \u2014 all are read-path/navigation/pagination items. Confirmed via direct issue-tracker search (no open issue for \\\"duplicate entries\\\" / \\\"idempot\\\" / \\\"backlog_groom duplicate\\\" matches this) and a full read of the contract doc.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Design decision: how should `backlog_groom(append=True)` detect a near-identical repeated write to the same section \u2014 e.g. exact/near-duplicate content-hash check against existing entries, or require callers to pass an idempotency key, or something else\\n- [ ] Whatever guard is chosen prevents the exact failure mode observed on #2953 (same agent role re-running the same grooming step against the same content and getting a fresh duplicate entry instead of a no-op or replace)\\n- [ ] Cleanup pass on #2953 itself: strike the duplicate entries via `backlog_strike_entry` once the write-path fix is in place, so its RT-ICA Final Pass / finalize step (per `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md`) can run against clean content\\n- [ ] Confirm whether this recurs outside the #2956 outage scenario \u2014 i.e. is this a general retry-safety gap (any write an agent can't confirm landed, then retries) or was the #2956 outage the only realistic trigger\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nDiscovered while orchestrating the #2953/#2956 tracing effort (see #2956, #3054, #2955 \\\"dh plugin working register\\\" for surrounding context). Not a duplicate of #3059 (that issue is about the *read-side* map response being unbounded, not write-side duplicate appends) \u2014 verified #3059's body directly, it describes `disclosure_handler.py`'s map assembly, unrelated mechanism.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix: backlog_groom has no idempotency/dedup guard against repeated near-identical appends** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\